WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
[CROWD NOISE]

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.800
[CROWD NOISE]

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.534
OK, Anna Wintour?

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:09.004
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:09.004 --> 00:00:14.390
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:14.890
 Hello.

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:20.740
I know many people are
curious about who I am

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:22.420
and how I approach my work.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:23.440
 OK, off the table.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.070
OK.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:25.660
 This is a class
for those who want

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:27.700
to understand my
leadership style

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.280
and then understand the
experiences that have helped me

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.870
become an effective leader.

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:34.420
Love that page-- triple,
triple thumbs up.

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:36.520
You need someone
who can push you

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:37.930
that isn't pulling you back.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:42.610
I do not believe
in micromanaging.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:44.380
It's important to
empower those that

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:47.200
are working with you
because you are nothing--

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.940
nothing without a good team.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:51.430
It's really, really important
to surround yourself

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:53.710
with a team whose
opinions that you trust,

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:55.810
who are not in
any way frightened

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:57.262
of disagreeing with you.

00:00:57.262 --> 00:00:58.220
And you have to listen.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:04.599
Possibly the most important
meeting that we have

00:01:04.599 --> 00:01:08.020
is the one that we have when we
all come back from the shows.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:11.170
I would love for you to come
with us to one of these fashion

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:13.210
meetings.

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:14.980
There is always a
time when you know

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:16.420
you have to break the rules.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.880
This cover was a deeply
controversial cover,

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.090
but Kim and Kanye were part of
the conversation of the day,

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:23.860
and for Vogue not to
recognize that would

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:25.510
have been a big misstep.

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:26.560
You are leading.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.700
You are not following.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.890
And that's a very
important lesson

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:31.360
to always keep in your mind.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:39.720
You are driven by your heart,
you are driven by your talent,

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.510
and you're driven
by your instinct.

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:43.948
And if you start
to question and look

00:01:43.948 --> 00:01:45.740
at what people are
doing to the left of you

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:47.640
or to the right of
you, you are going

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.220
to lose that clarity of thought.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:51.500
Listen to the information.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:55.280
In the end, it has to
come from who you are.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:01.220
Own your decisions, and own who
you are, but without apology.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:05.140
I'm Anna Wintour, and
this is my MasterClass.

